BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Hatefreetogether": "https://hatefreetogether.org/event/voting-from-different-perspectives-studying-elections-across-disciplines/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:hatefreetogether
X-SOURCE:Hate-Free Together
DTSTART;TZID=UTC:20261027T150000
DTEND;TZID=UTC:20261027T160000
DTSTAMP:20260910T205942Z
CREATED:20260910T205942Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T205942Z
UID:10000727-1793113200-1793116800@hatefreetogether.org
SUMMARY:Voting from Different Perspectives: Studying Elections across Disciplines
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Inclusive Excellence (Campus Community Book Project) \nThis panel brings together faculty from across UC Davis and UC Davis Health discuss their research on voting and elections within and between different disciplines as well as national and international contexts. The panel aims to share research\, advance research literacy\, and explore scholarly boundaries of expertise as well as areas for cross-pollination. \nPanelists will include: \n\nVikram D. Amar\, Daniel J. Dykstra Distinguished Professor of Law\nRuth Shim\, Director of Cultural Psychiatry and Luke & Grace Kim Professor in Cultural Psychiatry\, Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences\nLauren Young\, Associate Professor and Director of Graduate Studies\, Political Science\nMegan Macklin (moderator)\, Director of Campus Climate and Inclusion Initiatives\, Office of Campus and Community Relations/Inclusive Excellence\n\nYou must register in advance for this event.
URL:https://hatefreetogether.org/event/voting-from-different-perspectives-studying-elections-across-disciplines/
LOCATION:Virtual
CATEGORIES:Season of Connection
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hatefreetogether.org/wp-content/uploads/Books.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"UC Davis Library": "https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/2026-fall-data-sci-in-practice"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ucdavis_library
SUMMARY:Data Science in Practice (talk series)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T160000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54154289273101
DESCRIPTION:Beginning October 13\, join us at DataLab (Shields Library 362
 ) every other Tuesday from 3-4pm for Data Science in Practice -- interdisc
 iplinary talks featuring researchers from across the UC Davis community ab
 out how they’re using data\, data science methods\, and emerging technol
 ogies to tackle their work.\n\n \n\nThe Fall 2026 schedule is:\n\nOct 13 
 – Juan Tellez\, Political ScienceOct 27 – Tina Law\, SociologyNov 10 
 – Mike Oskin\, Earth and Planetary Sciences \n\nTogether we’ll discove
 r and learn from different perspectives on and approaches to data-driven r
 esearch. This series features a mix of talks on active and recently comple
 ted projects from academia\, government and industry in a friendly\, colle
 gial atmosphere. After the talks\, stick around to network with colleagues
  new and old over light refreshments. This series is organized by DataLab 
 staff and graduate student affiliates. \n\n \n\nAll members of the UC Davi
 s community (students\, staff\, faculty\, alumni) are welcome to attend. W
 e encourage you to attend in person! To attend remotely via Zoom\, please 
 register in advance.\n\n \n\nQuestions? Interested in presenting or becomi
 ng a DataLab affiliate? Contact us at datalab@ucdavis.edu.
LOCATION:Shields Library\, 362
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/2026-fall-data-sci-in-practic
 e
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
