X-SOURCE-ID:ucdavis_library
SUMMARY:Making Sense of Scientific Articles: A Survival Kit for Reading Re
 search Papers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T160000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54239696888321
DESCRIPTION:Struggling to make sense of scientific papers? You're not alon
 e! Scientific articles can be intimidating\, but knowing how to approach t
 hem makes a big difference.\n\nJoin students from the College of Biologica
 l Sciences' BioInnovation Group for a workshop designed to help you tackle
  scientific papers with confidence. Learn how to find research articles th
 at interest you\, navigate the different sections of a scientific paper\, 
 and break down complex research into your own words. We'll share practical
  tips and tricks to make reading scientific literature feel a little less 
 overwhelming.\n\nWhether you're reading papers for a class\, exploring a r
 esearch topic\, or just curious about scientific discoveries\, this worksh
 op will help you build skills you can use throughout your academic journey
 .
LOCATION:Shields Library\, 205
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/making-sense-of-scientific-ar
 ticles
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
